-- title:
--   Reducedness and finite type of the edge chart ring over W(k)/p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$; write $K_0$ for the quotient $W(k)/\mathfrak p$ of the Witt vectors of $k$ by [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.pIdeal p (WittVector p k)`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_SpecialFormalModule.html#L412), i.e. by the principal ideal generated by the image of $p$, and equip $K_0$ with a $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra structure (any such structure, given as a hypothesis). Let `chartERing ℤ_[p] (p : ℤ_[p]) p` denote the $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra obtained from `edgeQuot ℤ_[p] (p : ℤ_[p])`, the quotient of the polynomial ring `MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℤ_[p]` in two variables by the principal ideal generated by `edgeRel ℤ_[p] (p : ℤ_[p])`, by localising away from the element `edgeQuot.discr ℤ_[p] (p : ℤ_[p]) p`, the class of `edgeDiscr ℤ_[p] p`. The assertion is the conjunction of two statements about the base change $K_0 \otimes_{\mathbb Z_p} \mathrm{chartERing}\,\mathbb Z_p\,(p)\,p$: it is a $K_0$-algebra of finite type, and it is a reduced ring.
--
--   This is the ring-theoretic input, at the level of a single standard edge chart, for the special fibre of the Čerednik–Drinfeld model over $W(k)/p$; in the classical presentation the chart ring is $\mathbb Z_p[\xi,\eta]/(\xi\eta-p)$ localised away from the discriminant, whose reduction modulo $p$ is a localisation of $K_0[\xi,\eta]/(\xi\eta)$. It is used in the construction of a reduced, separated scheme, locally of finite type, representing the functor `omegaObj`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalOmega_finiteType_and_isReduced_tensorProduct_chartERing_of_isAlgClosed.lean

